<title>CANADA: Petro-Canada cuts posted oil prices.</title>
<headline>Petro-Canada cuts posted oil prices.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Petro-Canada said it lowered the price it would pay for some grades of crude oil by C$15.00/cubic metre or C$2.38/barrel, effective immediately.</p>
<p>The new prices were listed as follows: Edmonton light sweet C$196.00/cubic metre, or C$31.16/barrel Cromer light sour C$192.00/cubic metre, or C$30.53/barrel Hardisty medium C$173.00/cubic metre, or C$27.50/barrel -- Reuters Calgary Bureau 403 531-1624</p>
</text>
